# Cross-origin isolation for the worker page — step 7.8.
#
# Consumed by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify verbatim. **GitHub Pages ignores this
# file and cannot set response headers at all**, which is why it is not an
# option here: the page would deploy, load, and then report no WebGPU device
# with nothing in the console pointing at the host.
#
# WHY THESE HEADERS AT ALL
# COOP+COEP together make the page cross-origin isolated, which is what unlocks
# SharedArrayBuffer, which is what pthreads needs (D-0033). Without them the
# wasm worker fails at startup, not at first use — so a page that "loads fine"
# proves nothing.
#
# THE PART THAT BREAKS LATE (RISKS.md §1)
# `require-corp` applies to EVERY cross-origin subresource. The page fetches
# WGSL and assets from the coordinator on another origin, so those responses
# must each carry `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` — ACAO is not
# enough and fails with a console error that names CORS instead of COEP.
# Verified server-side on /kernel, /asset, /metrics, /metrics/stream, /render.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# The wasm binary must be served with the right type or streaming compilation
# silently falls back to the slow path.
/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

# ── DO NOT CACHE THE WORKER ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A cached module means the browser runs OLD code after a deploy, and there is
# nothing on screen to say so. A fix was deployed, verified byte-identical on
# the server, and the page kept aborting at the same line number for another
# round — because Safari was still executing the previous build.
#
# `no-cache` still revalidates rather than re-downloading 9 MB every load: the
# browser asks, and gets a 304 when nothing changed. What it cannot do is serve
# a stale module without checking.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
